\eqn{B = \sum_k \max(x_k - y_k, 0)} and \eqn{C = \sum_k \max(y_k - x_k,
0)} (what only the first and only the second has); Baselga (2013, 2017):\tabular{lll}{
   Function \tab Component \tab Formula \cr
   \code{bray()} \tab Bray-Curtis dissimilarity (total) \tab \eqn{\frac{B + C}{2A + B + C}} \cr
   \code{bray_balanced()} \tab balanced variation, \eqn{d_{BC-bal}} \tab \eqn{\frac{\min(B, C)}{A + \min(B, C)}} \cr
   \code{bray_gradient()} \tab abundance gradient, \eqn{d_{BC-gra}} \tab \eqn{d_{BC} - d_{BC-bal}} \cr
   \code{soergel()} \tab Ruzicka dissimilarity (total) \tab \eqn{\frac{B + C}{A + B + C}} \cr
   \code{soergel_balanced()} \tab balanced variation, \eqn{d_{RUZ-bal}} \tab \eqn{\frac{2\min(B, C)}{A + 2\min(B, C)}} \cr
   \code{soergel_gradient()} \tab abundance gradient, \eqn{d_{RUZ-gra}} \tab \eqn{d_{RUZ} - d_{RUZ-bal}} \cr
}


\code{\link[=soergel]{soergel()}} is the Ruzicka dissimilarity (vegan's quantitative Jaccard),
